OL,3,A'Tax rises needed to plug #35bn gap'
OL,4,Aand 'Putin breaks Trump's 'ceasefire"
OL,5,
OL,6,FMany of the front pages feature
OL,7,Freaction to US President Donald Trump's
OL,8,Fannouncement of an energy ceasefire
OL,9,Fbetween Ukraine and Russia. The
OL,10,FGuardian and the Times both highlight
OL,11,Fthe fact that Ukrainian President
OL,12,FVolodymyr Zelensky appeared to be
OL,13,Funaware of the truce before it was
OL,14,Fannounced. The Daily Telegraph leads on
OL,15,FZelensky's claims that Russia has
OL,16,Fcontinued to strike energy sites. The
OL,17,Fheadline is "Putin breaks Trump's
OL,18,F'ceasefire'". The paper's editorial
OL,19,Fargues that the main problem with the
OL,20,Fdeal is that it "only exists in the US
OL,21,FPresident's head".
OL,23,APub: 12-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/4
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,310,300,200,140,0,100
